# CODEOWNERS
#
# Each line is: path pattern, then one or more owners. The LAST matching line wins.
# Owners can be users (@name), teams (@org/team), or emails.
# Turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection so this is enforced.
# Place this file in the repo root, in docs/, or in .github/.
#
# Rules:
#   * Every folder should have an owner. Use teams, not single people.
#   * Keep at least 2 people in each team so reviews never block on one person.
#   * Review this file every quarter and when people change roles.

# Default owner for everything
*                           @[org]/[engineering]

# Application code
/src/api/                   @[org]/[backend]
/src/web/                   @[org]/[frontend]
/src/workers/               @[org]/[backend]

# Sensitive areas (2 approvals required by CONTRIBUTING.md)
/src/auth/                  @[org]/[security] @[org]/[backend]
/src/payments/              @[org]/[payments] @[org]/[security]
/migrations/                @[org]/[database] @[org]/[backend]

# Infrastructure and delivery
/infra/                     @[org]/[platform]
/Dockerfile                 @[org]/[platform]
/.github/workflows/         @[org]/[platform]

# Tests
/tests/                     @[org]/[qa] @[org]/[engineering]

# Documentation
/docs/                      @[org]/[engineering]
/docs/adr/                  @[org]/[tech_leads]
/SECURITY.md                @[org]/[security]
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md         @[org]/[project_managers]
/LICENSE                    @[org]/[legal]
/CHANGELOG.md               @[org]/[engineering] @[org]/[qa]

# ML work (remove if not used)
/docs/ml/                   @[org]/[ml]
/src/prompts/               @[org]/[ml]
